{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator", "label": "Spec 002 \u2014 Rule Evaluator sandboxado", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ordem vinda de docs/spec.md \u00a72.1 item 3: implementar o rule_evaluator sandboxado logo depois dos contratos \u2014 '\u00e9 pouco c\u00f3digo, mas \u00e9 o componente que mais d\u00f3i corrigir depois se nascer inseguro'. Regra dura: usar lib de JSONLogic, nunca eval de string livre."}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_rule_evaluator_py", "label": "rule_evaluator.py (desenho proposto)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_ruledecision", "label": "RuleDecision (desenho: effect, rule_id, message)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Carrega rule_id/message para o audit log: o AuditEvent do passo 001 j\u00e1 tem rule_id: str | None \u2014 este \u00e9 o valor que alimenta esse campo quando o interceptor (pr\u00f3ximo passo) registrar a decis\u00e3o. _StrictModel, frozen=True."}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_ruleevaluationerror", "label": "RuleEvaluationError (erro de config, n\u00e3o de neg\u00f3cio)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Condi\u00e7\u00e3o malformada n\u00e3o \u00e9 silenciosamente ignorada nem silenciosamente negada: \u00e9 erro de quem editou rules.yaml \u00e0 m\u00e3o \u2014 mesma filosofia do extra=forbid do passo 001, falhar alto no load/eval em vez de mascarar. Pular a regra quebrada silenciosamente \u00e9 pior: pode ser justo a regra que bloquearia algo perigoso."}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_json_logic_qubit", "label": "json-logic-qubit (depend\u00eancia do spec)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/qubitproducts/json-logic-py", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nota adicionada durante a implementa\u00e7\u00e3o: o pacote json-logic 'oficial' citado como exemplo pela spec est\u00e1 quebrado em Python 3 desde 2017 (tests.keys()[0] \u2192 TypeError reproduzido nos testes deste passo). json-logic-qubit \u00e9 o fork mantido que corrige isso; mesma API, ent\u00e3o nada no design muda."}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_jsonlogic", "label": "JsonLogic (jsonlogic.com)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://jsonlogic.com", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_sandbox_sem_eval", "label": "JSONLogic sandboxado, nunca eval", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "json_logic.jsonLogic(rule.condition, facts), nada de eval/exec. rule.condition j\u00e1 \u00e9 um dict estruturado (carregado do YAML, validado na forma pelo Pydantic) \u2014 a \u00fanica superf\u00edcie de execu\u00e7\u00e3o \u00e9 o conjunto fixo de operadores da JsonLogic. N\u00e3o h\u00e1 string livre em nenhum ponto do caminho."}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_first_match_wins", "label": "first-match-wins", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ordem importa: percorre ruleset.rules na ordem do YAML; a primeira regra cujo condition avalia truthy define o effect. \u00c9 o modelo mais simples de auditar \u2014 quem l\u00ea o rules.yaml de cima pra baixo entende a decis\u00e3o sem precisar somar prioridades num\u00e9ricas."}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_default_allow", "label": "Default ALLOW quando nenhuma regra casa", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "As Hard Rules s\u00e3o um punhado de regras que bloqueiam ou exigem aprova\u00e7\u00e3o para a\u00e7\u00f5es perigosas \u2014 modelo de firewall com exce\u00e7\u00f5es, n\u00e3o whitelist exaustiva. Alternativa rejeitada: default DENY inverteria para 's\u00f3 o que est\u00e1 explicitamente permitido roda', exigindo uma regra por skill/a\u00e7\u00e3o; mais seguro em tese, mas n\u00e3o \u00e9 o que a spec descreve. Se preferir default-deny, \u00e9 uma linha (default_effect vira par\u00e2metro) \u2014 mas decidir agora, n\u00e3o descobrir depois que uma a\u00e7\u00e3o devia ter sido bloqueada e passou por falta de regra."}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_hard_rules", "label": "3-5 Hard Rules", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Item 3 da \u00a72.1 do spec.md: punhado de regras espec\u00edficas que bloqueiam ou exigem aprova\u00e7\u00e3o para a\u00e7\u00f5es perigosas. As regras reais do cliente 1 ficam fora de escopo \u2014 n\u00e3o existe cliente 1 configurado no repo; este passo entrega o motor."}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_auditevent", "label": "AuditEvent (passo 001)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_interceptor_py", "label": "interceptor.py (\u00a72.1 item 4: allowlist SSRF, DLP, audit log)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fora de escopo deste passo; \u00e9 o passo seguinte. Ser\u00e1 quem registra a RuleDecision no audit log."}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_ruleprovider", "label": "RuleProvider (interface)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_yamlruleprovider", "label": "YamlRuleProvider (futuro)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fora de escopo: ainda n\u00e3o existe implementa\u00e7\u00e3o concreta de RuleProvider; este passo s\u00f3 consome o RuleSet j\u00e1 validado em mem\u00f3ria."}, {"id": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_ruleset", "label": "RuleSet", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_002_rule_evaluator", "target": "docs_readme_specs_dir", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_002_rule_evaluator", "target": "docs_readme_spec_md", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/specs/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": "docs/spec.md \u00a72.1, item 3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_002_rule_evaluator", "target": "specs_002_rule_evaluator_rule_evaluator_py", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", 